{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Make soft plastic recycling collection mandatory for large retailers",
        "additional_details": "Supermarkets running voluntary soft plastic take-back schemes show that collection is logistically achievable. What's missing is consistency across the retail sector. Making in-store soft plastic collection mandatory for larger shops would close that gap, reducing the volume reaching landfill, incineration, and ultimately our oceans, and would finally give the public a genuine, convenient way to dispose of this material responsibly.",
        "background": "Soft plastic (crisp packets, bread bags, film) can't be recycled at home and mostly ends up in landfill or incinerated. Mismanaged plastic also pollutes rivers and oceans, where it's ingested by fish, birds and marine life. Require all large shops to provide in-store recycling points.",
